WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.350
<v Speaker>Just a short lecture</v>

2
00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:03.570
around CloudFront geo restriction.

3
00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:06.210
So you can restrict who can access your distribution

4
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:08.010
based on the country where they

5
00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:10.140
try to access the distribution from.

6
00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:12.960
So you can set up an allow list to define a list

7
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.700
of approved countries,

8
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:18.060
or you can set up a block list to set up a list

9
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.980
of banned countries.

10
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.720
Now the country is determined

11
00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.780
by using a third party geo IP database to match the IP

12
00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.600
of the user to the country it belongs to.

13
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.690
So the use case for using geo restriction would be copyright

14
00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:33.900
laws to control access to content.

15
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:37.140
So in order to use the geographic protection,

16
